Third-party software
--------------------
Shipped packages depend only on permissively licensed software (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause,
BSD-3-Clause, ISC, 0BSD, MPL-2.0 unmodified); scripts/gates/check-licenses.mjs enforces this.

One data package is installed, never bundled, as a transitive of @lingui/core (through Babel's browserslist):
caniuse-lite, CC-BY-4.0; its licence file ships in the package (ADR-0160).

Optional packs may bundle, unmodified and loaded separately from the player, components under
weak copyleft licences. Their notices ship with the pack:
  - packs/layouts-elk      elkjs        EPL-2.0
  - packs/routing-libavoid libavoid-js  LGPL
